{"attachments":[],"author":{"display_name":"DM radar","id":"313689699627696139","is_bot":0,"username":"bfdm"},"author_id":"313689699627696139","channel_id":"736709568389709834","content":"The Ozark howler is a creature aberrated by Croatoan. This is a juvenile, and juveniles are harder to hit than adults. An adult has far more resistances (including to non-magical attacks) It can be greatly affected by any spell that removes mist from the area.\nAdult Howler Stats\nArmor Class 12 (Juvenile 16)\nHit Points 75\nSpeed 20 ft., fly 10 ft. (hover)\nSTR     22 (+6)\nDEX     10 (+0)\nCON     18 (+4)\nINT    7 (-3)    \nWIS    11(+0) \nCHA     20 (+5)\n\nSaving Throws STR+ 6, Cha +5\nDamage Resistances acid, fire, lightning, thunder; bludgeoning, piercing, and slashing from nonmagical attacks\nDamage Immunities cold, necrotic, poison\nCondition Immunities charmed, exhaustion, frightened, grappled, paralyzed, petrified, poisoned, prone, restrained\nSenses darkvision 60 ft., passive Perception 10\nEndurance. The Ozark Howler has advantage on Constitution saving throws against exhaustion.\n\nACTIONS\nThe howler can misty step 15 ft at will as her movement\nMultiattack. The Ozark Howler makes three attacks: one with its bite and two with its claws.","created_at":"2020-08-08T20:52:29.956000Z","edited_at":null,"id":"741760774778650696","reply_to_id":null,"thread":null,"thread_id":null}
